{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"1|# QG Project Instructions\\n2|\\n3|## Project\\n4|\\n5|```text\\n6|QG\\n7|/home/treshen/Projects/QG/\\n8|```\\n9|\\n10|QG is an existing, in-progress native Ubuntu/Linux video explorer and player.\\n11|Earlier manual Hermes runs may have advanced the implementation farther than the\\n12|control documents indicate. Use actual source, build, tests, and runtime evidence\\n13|when reconciling stale state.\\n14|\\n15|## Source of Truth\\n16|\\n17|Priority:\\n18|\\n19|```text\\n20|1. DESIGN.md\\n21|2. validated actual implementation behavior\\n22|3. DECISIONS.md\\n23|4. dev-guide.md\\n24|5. GUIDE_STATE.md\\n25|6. current task instruction\\n26|```\\n27|\\n28|`DESIGN.md` defines approved product behavior and architecture.\\n29|`dev-guide.md` defines the ordered implementation pipeline.\\n30|`GUIDE_STATE.md` records execution progress.\\n31|`DECISIONS.md` records durable architecture/implementation decisions.\\n32|`REQUIREMENTS_MATRIX.md` records requirement coverage.\\n33|\\n34|## Session Startup\\n35|\\n36|For a development turn:\\n37|\\n38|1. read `GUIDE_STATE.md`;\\n39|2. read relevant `DECISIONS.md`;\\n40|3. read relevant `REQUIREMENTS_MATRIX.md`;\\n41|4. locate the current/next work item in `dev-guide.md`;\\n42|5. read that work item in full;\\n43|6. read only the relevant `DESIGN.md` sections;\\n44|7. inspect the actual implementation/tests/build definitions required by that item.\\n45|\\n46|Use fresh filesystem evidence rather than conversational memory.\\n47|\\n48|## Existing-Project Rule\\n49|\\n50|Treat QG as an existing project.\\n51|Preserve compatible implementation.\\n52|When recorded state and actual implementation disagree, reconcile them using\\n53|source, build, tests, and runtime evidence before advancing.\\n54|\\n55|## Execution Model\\n56|\\n57|Continuous autonomous development is driven by:\\n58|\\n59|```text\\n60|/home/treshen/Projects/QG/hermes/qg-pipeline.py\\n61|```\\n62|\\n63|Each Hermes invocation executes exactly one work item:\\n64|\\n65|```text\\n66|select\\n67|→ mark IN_PROGRESS\\n68|→ inspect\\n69|→ implement\\n70|→ build\\n71|→ test\\n72|→ validate\\n73|→ persist state\\n74|→ exit\\n75|```\\n76|\\n77|The external runner launches the next fresh Hermes invocation.\\n78|\\n79|A work item is:\\n80|\\n81|- a development prompt;\\n82|- a mandatory checkpoint;\\n83|- FI-01 final integration;\\n84|- RV-01 release validation.\\n85|\\n86|## Completion Rules\\n87|\\n88|A work item becomes COMPLETE only when its completion criteria and validation\\n89|gate have actually passed.\\n90|\\n91|Validation evidence takes priority over stale status text.\\n92|A genuine external blocker sets the item and pipeline to BLOCKED with exact evidence.\\n93|The full pipeline becomes COMPLETE only after all prompts, checkpoints, FI-01,\\n94|and RV-01 pass.\\n95|\\n96|## Approved Architecture\\n97|\\n98|```text\\n99|C++20\\n100|Qt 6\\n101|Qt Quick / QML\\n102|Qt Quick Controls 2\\n103|C++ QAbstractItemModel / QAbstractListModel\\n104|Qt Quick Scene Graph\\n105|OpenGL\\n106|X11 / xcb\\n107|libmpv C API\\n108|mpv_render_context\\n109|SQLite\\n110|POSIX/Linux filesystem APIs\\n111|GIO / GVfs\\n112|UDisks2 / D-Bus where required\\n113|FFmpeg libraries\\n114|CMake\\n115|Ninja\\n116|CTest / Qt Test\\n117|native Ubuntu .deb packaging\\n118|```\\n119|\\n120|Architecture boundaries:\\n121|\\n122|```text\\n123|QML presentation\\n124|↓\\n125|C++ controllers/coordinators\\n126|↓\\n127|C++ models/services\\n128|↓\\n129|filesystem / persistence / playback / Linux integration\\n130|```\\n131|\\n132|Key invariants:\\n133|\\n134|- filesystem is authoritative for files/folders;\\n135|- application metadata is separate;\\n136|- one canonical ordered folder model/context drives Browse, Reel, Previous/Next,\\n137|  and auto-next;\\n138|- one heavy libmpv playback session exists;\\n139|- Stage and Cinema share that session;\\n140|- primary playback uses libmpv Render API integrated with Qt Quick/OpenGL;\\n141|- GUI/render threads remain responsive;\\n142|- high-volume state lives in C++ models;\\n143|- background work is bounded, cancellable, and stale-proof;\\n144|- native Linux file behavior is preserved.\\n145|\\n146|## Implementation Discipline\\n147|\\n148|Inspect existing files and direct dependencies before editing.\\n149|Use actual existing API/type names.\\n150|Keep one development work item per automated Hermes invocation.\\n151|Run focused tests first, then the work item's broader validation gate.\\n152|Use temporary/disposable filesystem fixtures for destructive file-operation tests.\\n153|Keep `GUIDE_STATE.md` concise.\\n154|Update `DECISIONS.md` only for durable decisions.\\n155|Update `REQUIREMENTS_MATRIX.md` only when requirement state materially changes.\\n156|\\n157|## Local Filesystem Workflow\\n158|\\n159|This project uses the local project filesystem directly.\\n160|Hermes filesystem checkpoints are enabled by the external runner with\\n161|`--checkpoints`.\\n162|\\n163|## Runner Output\\n164|\\n165|When invoked by `qg-pipeline.py`, the final non-empty response line is one of:\\n166|\\n167|```text\\n168|QG_RUNNER_RESULT=CONTINUE\\n169|QG_RUNNER_RESULT=BLOCKED\\n17...", "duration_ms": 131, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791453317295}
