{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"240|- Selecting a card does **not** start playback. Double-click / Enter starts it.\\n241|\\n242|### 3.5 Resizing and responsive behavior\\n243|\\n244|| Window width | Sidebar | Columns / density | Reel | Context strip |\\n245||---|---|---|---|---|\\n246|| ≥ 1500 | Panel (240) | Auto columns, target card 240 | Side panel | Full |\\n247|| 1150–1500 | Rail (56) | Auto columns, target 220 | Overlay drawer | Full |\\n248|| 900–1150 | Rail (56) | Auto columns, target 200 | Overlay drawer | Compact (name + order) |\\n249|| 700–900 | Hidden (overlay) | 2–3 columns, target 190 | Overlay drawer | Hidden |\\n250|| < 700 | Hidden | 1–2 columns; Compact rows preferred | Overlay drawer | Hidden |\\n251|\\n252|Column count is `max(1, floor((content_width - gutters) / (min_card + gap)))` with `min_card = 168` and `max_card = 320`. Cards never stretch beyond `max_card`; extra width becomes gutters at the row edges (centered), not stretched thumbnails. This preserves thumbnail aspect on ultrawide displays.\\n253|\\n254|### 3.6 Status/context areas\\n255|\\n256|- The **context strip** answers \\\"what folder, how much, in what order.\\\"\\n257|- The **status strip** answers \\\"what's selected, is anything busy, did something just happen.\\\" Background work is surfaced as a quiet cluster of animated dots plus a count; clicking it opens a small popover listing running tasks (thumbnailing, probing, trashing) with counts, never blocking the UI.\\n258|- Transient messages (rename succeeded, moved to Trash, thumbnail failed) appear as **toasts** anchored bottom-center of the content surface, auto-dismiss after 4s, with an **Undo** affordance for Trash.\\n259|\\n260|---\\n261|\\n262|## 4. Main Window Wireframe\\n263|\\n264|Normal first-open / browser state (annotated). Wide layout, Standard density.\\n265|\\n266|```text\\n267|┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────