{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"780|### 11.4 Bulk actions\\n781|\\n782|Multi-select enables bulk Favorite / Watched / Cut / Copy / Trash. Bulk Trash reports progress per item in the status strip and offers a single Undo. A partial failure in a bulk operation produces a result summary toast: `Moved 9 of 10 to Trash — 1 permission error` with a \\\"Details\\\" expansion, never a modal per item.\\n783|\\n784|---\\n785|\\n786|## 12. Empty / Error / Loading States\\n787|\\n788|All states follow the same shape: **glyph + one-line truth + one-line explanation + one primary action**, centered in the content surface, on `--surface-0`, without illustration noise. The wording never lies: an empty folder is \\\"empty,\\\" a permission problem says so, and a disconnected drive says which one.\\n789|\\n790|| State | Glyph / color | Headline | Body | Primary action |\\n791||---|---|---|---|---|\\n792|| **Empty directory** | dimmed filmstrip | `This folder is empty` | `No videos or subfolders here.` | `Go to Home` |\\n793|| **Folder-only directory** | *no empty state* | — | The grid shows the child folders; the context strip reads `0 videos · N folders`. The string \\\"No videos found\\\" is **forbidden** here. | — |\\n794|| **No videos but subfolders** | dimmed filmstrip | *(none — folders render)* | Folders are a valid result and are shown normally. | — |\\n795|| **Access denied** | amber lock | `You don't have permission to open this folder` | `Try opening it as the owner, or check its permissions.` | `Properties` · `Copy path` |\\n796|| **Missing / disconnected drive** | amber plug-slash | `\\\"Old HDD\\\" is not connected` | `Reconnect the drive and QG will resume.` | `Retry` · `Eject` |\\n797|| **Loading (enumeration)** | animated ring | *(no headline)* | A skeleton grid of placeholder cards appears immediately; a thin indeterminate bar sits under the Path Bar. Existing interaction (sidebar, Path Bar, search entry) stays live. | — |\\n798|| **Loading (partial)** | — | — | Entries stream in in batches; a `Loading…` line remains at the grid's end until enumeration completes. | `Cancel` |\\n799|| **Search: no results** | dimmed magnifier | `No matches for \\\"xyz\\\"` | *(scope line)* | `Clear search` · `Search subfolders (soon)` |\\n800|| **Thumbnail failure** | amber filmstrip-slash | *(in-card)* | Tooltip: `Thumbnail couldn't be generated.` | `Retry` (context menu) |\\n801|| **Media probe failure** | amber dot on duration chip | duration shows `--:--` | Tooltip explains; playback still offered (mpv may still open it). | `Play anyway` |\\n802|| **Playback failure** | coral warning in Stage | `Can't play this file` | `The file may be corrupted, unsupported, or on a disconnected volume.` | `Open With…` · `Reveal in Folder` · `Next` |\\n803|| **Operation error (rename/trash/move)** | coral | short cause | recovery hint | context action + `Dismiss` |\\n804|\\n805|Design notes:\\n806|\\n807|- **Loading never blocks.** The skeleton grid is interactive; sidebar navigation and search remain available; navigating away cancels the pending enumeration.\\n808|- **Errors are recoverable, not terminal.** Every error state offers at least one action that moves the user forward.\\n809|- Unknown/decoding errors surface the underlying message in a collapsible \\\"Details\\\" area, because Linux users expect to read the real error.\\n810|\\n811|---\\n812|\\n813|## 13. Keyboard and Focus Model\\n814|\\n815|### 13.1 Focus model\\n816|\\n817|Three independent concepts, deliberately separated:\\n818|\\n819|- **Focus** (cyan ring) — the keyboard cursor; moves with arrows/Tab; determines where typing and shortcuts apply.\\n820|- **Selection** (signal border) — the action target; set by click/Space/Ctrl+click/Shift+range; what the status strip and menu describe.\\n821|- **Playback state** (mint) — independent of both; playback continues while you browse elsewhere.\\n822|\\n823|This separation is what makes QG usable without a mouse: you can browse (focus) while a file is selected and a different one is playing.\\n824|\\n825|### 13.2 Shortcut map\\n826|\\n827|**Navigation**\\n828|\\n829|| Action | Shortcut |\\n830||---|---|\\n831|| Back / Forward | `Alt+←` / `Alt+→` |\\n832|| Parent directory | `Alt+↑` or `Backspace` |\\n833|| Refresh | `F5` or `Ctrl+R` |\\n834|| Focus location / path entry | `Ctrl+L` |\\n835|| Go Home | `Alt+Home` |\\n836|| Places panel toggle | `F9` |\\n837|| Reel toggle | `Ctrl+R`… *(conflict)* → see note |\\n838|\\n839|> **Note on conflicts.** `Ctrl+R` is a natural \\\"refresh\\\" in file managers *and* a natural \\\"context panel\\\" in players. QG resolves it deliberately: **`F5` = refresh**, **`Ctrl+R` = toggle Reel**, and `Ctrl+L` = location. `Alt+↑` plus `Backspace` both go to parent (Nautilus and Windows Explorer agree on Backspace). This is documented in-app under Help → Shortcuts.\\n840|\\n841|**Search**\\n842|\\n843|| Action | Shortcut |\\n844||---|---|\\n845|| Search current folder | `Ctrl+F` |\\n846|| Clear search (keep focus) | `Esc` |\\n847|| Leave search / restore browse | `Esc` again, or `Cancel` |\\n848|\\n849|**Selection & o...", "duration_ms": 10, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791453347293}
{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"205|\\n206|Six regions, top-to-bottom / left-to-right by priority:\\n207|\\n208|1. **Title bar / app identity** — thin; the window uses a normal decorated title bar where the compositor provides one (no custom client-side decoration in MVP). QG does not fight the WM.\\n209|2. **Places sidebar** — left. Collapses between a **56px icon rail** and a **240px panel**.\\n210|3. **Path Bar** — the full-width anchor row: back / forward / parent / refresh, breadcrumbs (or a path entry), and the right cluster (search, order, density, overflow).\\n211|4. **Context strip** — one slim row under the Path Bar: current folder name, item counts, active order, view density. It collapses entirely when the window is narrow.\\n212|5. **Content surface** — center. Hosts Browse grid, Manifest search results, or the Stage. This is the only region whose content model changes.\\n213|6. **Reel** — right. Ordered list of the containing folder's videos; opens when playback starts, dismissible, remembers per session.\\n214|7. **Status strip** — bottom. Selection count, aggregate size, free space of the current volume, background-activity indicator, and transient status text.\\n215|\\n216|### 3.2 Toolbar/header behavior\\n217|\\n218|There is no conventional toolbar. This is deliberate: a toolbar row is the single strongest \\\"web app in a window\\\" signal, and it consumes vertical space that thumbnails want. Instead:\\n219|\\n220|- **Navigation** lives at the left of the Path Bar (icon buttons: back, forward, parent, refresh).\\n221|- **Search** is a field that occupies the breadcrumb track when activated.\\n222|- **Order**, **Density**, and **Overflow** are grouped at the right edge of the Path Bar.\\n223|- **Primary verbs** for the current selection appear contextually — in the card hover chip and in the Reel footer — never as permanent buttons.\\n224|\\n225|The Path Bar therefore behaves as *both* the toolbar and the location interface. This is the main \\\"own identity\\\" decision for the window chrome.\\n226|\\n227|### 3.3 Sidebar behavior\\n228|\\n229|- Two states: **rail** (56px, icons + tooltips) and **panel** (240px, icon + label, grouped).\\n230|- Groups, in order: **Pinned** (favorites/bookmarks), **Places** (Home, Videos, Downloads, Desktop, Documents), **Devices** (mounted volumes from `/proc/self/mountinfo` + GVfs), **Recent** (last locations, capped).\\n231|- A removable drive shows an eject affordance on hover; a disconnected drive shows an amber badge and greys out, remaining clickable to explain how to remount.\\n232|- The sidebar auto-collapses to a rail below 1100px and hides fully below 820px, where it becomes an overlay summoned from the Path Bar's leading button. The chosen width persists.\\n233|- Drag a folder onto the sidebar to pin it; drag out to reveal.\\n234|\", \"total_lines\": 1907, \"file_size\": 139848, \"truncated\": true, \"hint\": \"Use offset=235 to continue reading (showing 205-234 of 1907 lines)\", \"is_binary\": false, \"is_image\": false, \"not_found\": false}", "duration_ms": 9, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791453347297}
