ate). The component renders free space correctly from an injected value (verified by the QML test); end-to-end volume free space awaits a volume-stats source.\\n+- Next dependency-ready item: **CP-C** (Visual Browser Checkpoint).\\n+\\n ## Known Issues / Environment Fragility\\n \\n - **`qg_watcher` test is temp-filesystem-dependent.** `tst modelDiffPreservesUnaffectedRows` (P12) removes `gone.mp4` then creates `added.mp4`; on a filesystem that **reuses the just-freed inode** (observed on ext4 — e.g. the Hermes agent scratch `TMPDIR` under `/home`), the two files collide on inode identity, so `computeFolderDiff` classifies the change as `dataChanged` instead of remove+add and `removed.count()` is 0. On `/tmp` (tmpfs, no immediate inode reuse) the test passes. This is test-fixture fragility, **not** a product regression: identity-keyed diffing is per DESIGN §17.5/§17.8, and the recorded P12 PASS is valid under the standard environment.\\n\", \"files_modified\": [\"/home/treshen/Projects/QG/GUIDE_STATE.md\"], \"lint\": {\"status\": \"skipped\", \"message\": \"No linter for .md files\"}, \"resolved_path\": \"/home/treshen/Projects/QG/GUIDE_STATE.md\"}", "duration_ms": 142, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791454782382}
